<quiz>
  <question type="stack">

    <name>
      <text>Shared: Complete a partially filled linear-relation table</text>
    </name>


    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;
A linear relation is written as
\[
y-({@c@})={@m@}x.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Complete the three missing values in the table.
Some values have already been provided to help
you check the pattern.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;table border="1"
       cellpadding="8"
       style="border-collapse:collapse;
              text-align:center;"&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
  &lt;th&gt;\(x\)&lt;/th&gt;
  &lt;td&gt;\({@x1@}\)&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;td&gt;\({@x2@}\)&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;td&gt;\({@x3@}\)&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;td&gt;\({@x4@}\)&lt;/td&gt;
  &lt;td&gt;\({@x5@}\)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
  &lt;th&gt;\(y\)&lt;/th&gt;

  &lt;td&gt;
    \({@y1@}\)
  &lt;/td&gt;

  &lt;td&gt;
    [[input:ans1]]
    [[validation:ans1]]
    [[feedback:prt1]]
  &lt;/td&gt;

  &lt;td&gt;
    \({@y3@}\)
  &lt;/td&gt;

  &lt;td&gt;
    [[input:ans2]]
    [[validation:ans2]]
    [[feedback:prt2]]
  &lt;/td&gt;

  &lt;td&gt;
    [[input:ans3]]
    [[validation:ans3]]
    [[feedback:prt3]]
  &lt;/td&gt;

&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Remember that the equation is not yet written
with \(y\) by itself.
&lt;/p&gt;
      </text>
    </questiontext>


    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text>&lt;h3&gt;Worked solution&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
The given relation is
\[
y-({@c@})={@m@}x.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
First isolate \(y\) by adding \({@c@}\)
to both sides:
\[
y={@m@}x+({@c@}).
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
For \(x={@x2@}\):
\[
y=({@m@})({@x2@})+({@c@})
={@y2@}.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
For \(x={@x4@}\):
\[
y=({@m@})({@x4@})+({@c@})
={@y4@}.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
For \(x={@x5@}\):
\[
y=({@m@})({@x5@})+({@c@})
={@y5@}.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Therefore the completed row is
\[
{@y1@},\;
{@y2@},\;
{@y3@},\;
{@y4@},\;
{@y5@}.
\]
&lt;/p&gt;
      </text>
    </generalfeedback>


